- The 16-item Increment-A allowlist is exactly preserved. Removing the two required insertions reproduces the preimage only after normalizing carriage returns; raw source equality fails.
- The helper matches the prescribed logic and literal errors. It reloads/checks the checkpoint, reloads every stored reference, checks record equality, strictly prior round, discovery-plan identity, PIT scope, and semantic mode, then counts only `invalid` records carrying the reserved failure code. There is no catch or fallback that turns repository failures into zero.
- The unchanged `SearchProjectionV5.__post_init__` binds stored references to checkpoint record references and prohibits records without a checkpoint. The recovery path constructs stored records from those committed references. `StoredExperimentRecordV5` binds record hash/path to its reference. The unchanged `load_experiment` authenticates canonical record content and validates the render-rejection journal/event/payload authority; `load_checkpoint` is read-only. These seams support counting committed, authenticated records.
- The single new literal failure metric is guarded by a nonzero count and appended after the entire parent-episode loop, before archive-family and history evidence. Existing `evidence.add` calls retain their source text and relative order. The helper is adjacent to `_investigator_parts`; no additional functional changes appear in the preimage-to-current source comparison.
- The broad worktree already contains unrelated modified files. The task-specific preimage and diff support the two-insertion functional scope in `production_runtime.py`; the current worktree status alone cannot attribute unrelated changes to Task 2.
- Review used static source, diff, hash, and raw-text inspection only. No tests, synthetic inputs, probes, candidates, records, events, wrappers, requests, API/model/credential/evaluator/campaign calls, commits, pushes, or deployments were performed.

The quality failure concerns the explicit preservation defect and inaccurate verification claim. No additional functional defect was identified in the requested helper or evidence insertion.
